      ],
      "acceptable_supporting": []
    },
    "description": "Regal's compliance clients need to export every matching audit event from a rapidly growing, continuously changing event table. The current endpoint accepts an offset and page size, so deep exports repeatedly scan earlier rows, while concurrent inserts can shift records across page boundaries and cause the client to export duplicates or omit events. The service must keep responses bounded, preserve the requested tenant, event type, date range, and ordering throughout an export, and allow a client to resume after a disconnect without restarting from the beginning. Replace numeric offsets with a one-page response containing an opaque continuation value. The server must validate that the value represents the same query scope and resolve the next position from a stable unique ordering key rather than from a row count. The external representation should contain only the event summary fields needed by export consumers and must not leak the internal event entity or persistence query implementation.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide how a large, changing collection should expose bounded pages that can be traversed and resumed consistently without shifting records between pages.",
    "notes": "cursor-pagination fits the opaque continuation value with stable ordering keys; data-transfer-object covers the page payload and record-set the tabular-result reading."
  },
